(* Tests for the key id in PascalApi.Jwt (SignHS256 with a kid, ReadKid) and
  for PascalApi.JwtKeys (the static key ring, JWT_KEYS, signing and
  verifying by kid, the legacy secret, NotAfter, the lifetime rules of Sign).

  The token with a kid is checked against Python's hmac (header
  {"alg":"HS256","typ":"JWT","kid":"k1"}, jwt.io's claims and secret). Time
  comes from a fixed clock installed in TClock. A rotation is two rings: the
  old one signs, the new one (a new first key, the old key after it)
  verifies.

  DUnitX master. The FPCUnit mirror (tests/Unit/fpc) is generated by
  tools/gen_fpc_mirror.py; never edit the mirror by hand. *)

